statement:
Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and $C$ a smooth connected curve over $k$ [def-sc-curves] (nonempty, connected, of dimension one, separated, of finite type and smooth over $k$). Then:

1. $C$ is a Noetherian integral scheme [def-pc-integral-scheme]; let $\eta$ be its generic point, so that $k(C)=\mathcal O_{C,\eta}$ is a field [def-sc-function-field] and, for every nonempty open $V\subseteq C$ and every $x\in C$, the restriction maps $\mathcal O_C(V)\to\mathcal O_{C,x}\to\mathcal O_{C,\eta}=k(C)$ are injective;
2. every point of $C$ other than $\eta$ is a closed point, and $C$ has at least one closed point;
3. for every closed point $P$ of $C$ the local ring $\mathcal O_{C,P}$ is a discrete valuation ring whose fraction field is $k(C)$ (via the injection of 1.); we write $v_P:k(C)^*\to\mathbf Z$ for its normalized valuation.
